#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "40486856-137f-55c4-8464-f99e7e1c659f" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f66adb06-44ad-563b-ac24-9ab6372d2035" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131727} {:answer/id #uuid "08cdccd8-37ae-5add-81cd-fccd7a6665b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131728} {:answer/id #uuid "1993ae02-9b3f-5000-958c-8aa3b5491aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131729} {:answer/id #uuid "3e884146-7502-514c-bf6b-77b7f1225c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131730} {:answer/id #uuid "7fbdcd5c-9168-5e0c-abcc-e70739d4ebac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1993ae02-9b3f-5000-958c-8aa3b5491aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131729} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a558f56-23aa-5d01-8ee2-656291b19b0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a39392dd-970e-5bc4-92f4-87da19dde1bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-40437" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}6x\\,dy]dA,\n$$\n\nEvaluate the repeated integral above given that $D$ is a region in the $xz$-plane bounded by the lines $z=0,$ $x=0,$ and the curve $z+{x}^{2}=4.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $y,$ treating $x$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{4}6x\\,dy]dA & ={∬}_{D}6x[y]_{y={x}^{2}}^{y=4}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}6x(4-{x}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate this double integral, we plot $D$ as a type I plane region in the $xz$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14063571/assets/612c4fda39f7003024c322b6d1fa5c279815923905c8d023547a3be6b4a6805a.png)\n\nTherefore, to evaluate our double integral as a repeated integral over this region, we integrate with respect to $z$ and then with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}24x-6{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(24x-6{x}^{3})[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(24x-6{x}^{3})(4-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}96x-48{x}^{3}+6{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[48{x}^{2}-12{x}^{4}+{x}^{6}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(192-192+64)-0 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
